{
  "_": [
    "THE RENDER MATRIX, run by both ports against these same expectations:",
    "ts/test/render-matrix.test.ts and go/cmd/aontu/render_matrix_test.go.",
    "Every expectation here was obtained by running both CLIs and requiring",
    "them to agree (docs/contributing/testing.md, 'The parity probe').",
    "",
    "A case writes `files` into a fresh directory and walks its `steps`. A",
    "step either runs `aontu render` with `args`, or `edit`s, `remove`s or",
    "`chmod`s files in place. Before comparing, a runner rewrites the",
    "directory as {dir}, turns \\ into / so Windows agrees, and rewrites",
    "the package version as {version}: the two ports carry their own",
    "version series, which is the one field they never match on.",
    "",
    "`after` is EXHAUSTIVE. It is every file the directory holds at the",
    "end, the case's own `files` aside, so a port that writes one more",
    "than the other fails even when both wrote the listed ones correctly.",
    "The runtime's own `.jostraca/` record is the one exclusion: its log",
    "carries the time of the run. `afterMode` asks for a file's permission",
    "bits, and a case marked `posix` is skipped where they mean nothing.",
    "",
    "One behaviour stays out, and stays in the per-port tests: an I/O",
    "refusal, whose prose each generator runtime writes for itself."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "one-file-to-the-path",
      "files": {
        "gen.aontu": "out: file(\"zed.txt\", [\"foo = BAR\"])\n"
      },
      "steps": [
        {
          "args": [
            "{dir}/gen.aontu",
            "{dir}/out/one.txt"
          ],
          "code": 0,
          "out": "",
          "err": ""
        }
      ],
      "after": {
        "out/one.txt": "foo = BAR\n"
      }
    },
    {
